  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Exact: the 8-point parity gadget of UNATE-20261111-001 is a valid knot space of genus 4 with a Kasteleyn law under an independent check (fresh code, canonical K1-K3: every line and the four-point parity relation are knots). In a capped exact search of 281 lattice tori and 1,200 random knot spaces steered to genus 1 to 3, parity first occurs at genus 1: the 8-point lattice torus (2,0,4) computes three-input parity in its most constrained class; 16 of 281 lattice tori do.",
